        "original_id": "7f4c3475-8f39-5170-8715-eb17a137c09b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: The Joy Formidable, Sixpence None the Richer\n- Releases: A Balloon Called Moaning, The Big Roar, A Heavy Abacus, Whirring\n- Places: North Wales, London, England, New Braunfels, Texas, Nashville, Tennessee\n- Topics: alternative rock, Christian rock, discography, chart performance\n\nFacts:\n- The Joy Formidable is a Welsh alternative rock band that formed in 2007 in North Wales and is currently based in London, England.\n- Sixpence None the Richer, also known as Sixpence, is an American alternative Christian rock band that formed in New Braunfels, Texas, and later settled in Nashville, Tennessee.\n- The Joy Formidable released its debut extended play, \"A Balloon Called Moaning\", in December 2008.\n- The Joy Formidable released its debut studio album, \"The Big Roar\", in January 2011.\n- The Big Roar reached No. 31 on the UK Albums Chart.\n- \"A Heavy Abacus\" is the fifth and final single from The Joy Formidable's debut album, The Big Roar, and it was released in July 2011.\n- The Big Roar produced the single \"Whirring\", which reached No. 7 on the US Alternative Songs Chart.\n- The Big Roar produced the single \"A Heavy Abacus\", which reached No. 25 on the US Alternative Songs Chart.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
